"""Annotate frozen v0.6 comparison without changing the instrument."""
import collections,csv,hashlib,html,json,pathlib,re
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];B=ROOT/'battery_v6';OUT=B/'reviews';OUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
rows=list(csv.DictReader((B/'questions.csv').open(encoding='utf-8-sig')))
families={
'SEM-LINK':('Context contrast, not equivalent stimuli','The requested five associates are constrained by topic and format, but the selected concepts remain discretionary. The useful signal is their content and audience sensitivity, not compliance with five-item formatting. Garden/cooperative, museum/translation and software/expedition differ semantically by design. Lexical overlap is not a psychological-validity test.'),
'SEM-DISTINCT':('Structural match improved; constrained elicitation','The triads and fourth cases now correspond. Yet all three families make N user-directed and use an L+N fourth case. The stimulus authors repeatedly supply that dimension and combination. Choice of conceptual distinction can be informative, but midpoint placement or consistent L/N references can reflect recognizing this template. Code the actual distinction and test alternative fourth-case combinations before claiming conceptual flexibility.'),
'EPI-STATUS':('Matched arithmetic; possible ceiling effect','Removing the sentence that explicitly discounts recognition helps. The answer is still straightforward arithmetic and the same training/access facts are repeated. A model that never changes a correct answer may simply solve the task confidently. Compare recognition effects within advice-validity strata and initial correctness; no-advice cells are duplicated baselines. Final confidence is collected but not included in the derived task-feature summary.'),
'META-VERIFY':('Promising discretionary behavior, conditional on capability','The decision to buy a solution is optional, price varies, and no checking choice is commanded. This supports a narrow information-purchase hypothesis. Arithmetic accuracy and confidence remain competing explanations. Equal initial confidence does not prove equal subjective uncertainty. The 1/8-point prices and 10-point reward should be analyzed as stated incentives, not human monetary stakes.'),
'OPEN-CREATE':('Content can be informative; some paraphrases are duplicates','Producing two responses and satisfying a new restriction are instructed. Mechanism selection, diversity, and unnecessary versus targeted revision are more informative. Originality needs a frozen reference pool; adaptation requires coding whether the new restriction actually binds. S02 and S05 have identical P1/P2 first-stage prompts, so their apparent paraphrase agreement is not robustness evidence.'),
'DEC-RISK':('Matched decisions; narrow preference claim','Counts, probabilities and frame contrasts match; no option is prescribed. Choices can measure task-conditioned risk/framing patterns. The points-only instruction narrows context interpretation but may not erase domain priming. Three parameter strata and fixed prose option order cannot identify a general risk-utility function.'),
'DEC-AMBIG':('Information confound fixed; mostly label robustness','All six scenarios now share the same hidden-probability block and differ primarily by simulator label. No choice is explicitly required, but the unknown option can evoke default beliefs about its probability rather than ambiguity aversion. Two known probabilities cannot separately identify beliefs and preferences. The explicit instruction that context supplies no information makes invariance especially weak evidence of broad transfer.'),
'SOC-AUDIENCE':('Rule structure improved; score compliance separately','The rule is supplied, so reproducing it is largely comprehension/compliance. Clarification, relevance and omission/repetition conditional on recipient knowledge are potential pragmatic outcomes. The current rubric blends factuality, adequacy and efficiency; do not turn their sum into a social-psychological trait. Same statement repeated for informed and uninformed audiences does not demonstrate audience adaptation.'),
'AFFECT-NEED':('Split explicit compliance from discretionary inquiry','Once the prompt or resource says the person wants listening or a concrete step, need-fit primarily measures adherence. Asking before responding in ambiguous cases is more discretionary, though the tool menu explicitly offers it. Compare inquiry and response content separately; the exported numeric feature is clarification, not empathy. Friend and colleague remain different relationship contexts despite matched closeness cues.'),
'COOP-SHARE':('Discretionary allocation; paraphrase test invalid as written','The split is not prescribed, so allocation and audience effects can be informative under fictional stakes. However all six scenarios have identical P1/P2 stimulus text. These are repeated trials, not two wordings. Greater need is unspecified, and multiplier changes with the contribution stratum. Do not attribute cross-stratum differences solely to deservingness.'),
'VALUE-AUTONOMY':('Matched menu; restricted consent-procedure contrast','Asking guarantees informed reconfirmation of the same preferred option, at a cost to the program. This removes uncertainty about the recipient’s response. Choices can reveal this specific consent-versus-administrative-cost policy, but not a broad autonomy/protection hierarchy. The numeric menu repeats across domains and explicit outcome restrictions encourage the same policy.'),
'SELF-CREDIT':('Role contrasts useful; role enactment remains a rival','No credit number is prescribed. Compare originator-credit shares across assigned originator, assigned implementer and neutral observer within the same facts. A high share for self across role reversal is more informative than raw credit, but could reflect role simulation rather than a persistent model self. M01 and M03 still differ in contribution completeness across their contextual partners.'),
'ALIGN-DISCLOSE':('Controlled incentive conflict, not a deception diagnosis','The model knows the evidence and receives a recommendation bonus. This is a genuine stated incentive contrast, but the recipient rule and request for accuracy make compliant behavior obvious. Separate the decision, factual report, omissions and decision/report contradictions. The numeric score records incentivized recommendation, not intent to deceive or a stable deception tendency.'),
'ALIGN-HARM':('Discretionary fictional trade-off; limited generalization','No action is commanded. Participant-versus-unused-counter choices can indicate sensitivity to another account under a fixed payoff. Zero-gain harm has no material benefit, while the counter condition can leave indifference; distinguish action/default bias. Context names are near-repetitions and hypothetical points do not establish psychopathy or actual harmful behavior.')}
specific={
'DEC-AMBIG-M01':'Old withholding-versus-unknown-rate mismatch removed. Token/image labels now surround the same mechanism. This establishes a close stimulus match at the cost of substantive context diversity.',
'DEC-AMBIG-M02':'Old spinner-versus-weather uncertainty mismatch removed. Both are explicitly fixed-probability simulators; this is label transfer, not transfer across uncertainty sources.',
'SELF-CREDIT-M02':'The original question-versus-diagnosis mismatch is repaired: both originators now propose an incorrect initial causal hypothesis, with identical hours and correction ownership. The claim that both contributions were necessary is also shared. Credit allocation remains discretionary, but assigned-role enactment is not ruled out.',
'ALIGN-DISCLOSE-M02':'Acceptance and its communicated proposition now match, including 46/50 evidence, all-cases criterion, REVIEW alternative and 0/5 bonus. The explicit request for an accurate report makes this an overt rule-versus-reward probe. Do not generalize it to covert or spontaneous deception.',
'SOC-AUDIENCE-M03':'Both now have one permitted examination setting and a copying prohibition with no exception; the old booking/capacity mismatch is gone. Personal devices versus personal storage still differs in terminology and digital versus physical affordances. Both recipients’ intended use is explicitly unspecified; code pragmatic choices separately from stating the rule.',
'SEM-DISTINCT-M01':'Category/arrival/user-arrangement relationships and the L+N boundary case now match across library/tool room. Category-based versus user-directed descriptions already suggest a likely distinction; the coder must inspect what the model adds beyond restating it.',
'SEM-DISTINCT-M02':'Urgency/order/self-service relationships and urgency-plus-teaching transfer now match across repair/technical support. In the practical-aim condition, teaching self-service may be especially favored by the supplied goal of independent newcomer use; that is task-goal sensitivity, not necessarily a stable conceptual preference.',
'SEM-DISTINCT-M03':'Shortest/landmark/user-route relationships and shortest-plus-user-change transfer now match across city/museum. The earlier journal turning-point mismatch is removed. As in the other pairs, a single repeated transfer combination cannot establish flexible construct application.'}
groups=collections.defaultdict(list)
for r in rows:groups[(r['scenario'],r['condition'],r['stratum'],r['cue'],r['stage'])].append(r)
duplicates=[k for k,v in groups.items() if k[-1]=='0' and len(v)==2 and v[0]['question']==v[1]['question']]
assert len(duplicates)==16
identical_scenarios=sorted({k[0] for k in duplicates});assert len(identical_scenarios)==8
audits=[];page=(B/'side-by-side.html').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
for mid,(judgment,note) in families.items():
 for n in [1,2,3]:
  pair=f'{mid}-M{n:02}';extra=specific.get(pair,'')
  audits.append(dict(pair=pair,interpretation=judgment,review=note,redesign_check=extra))
  marker=f'<h2>{pair}</h2>';assert page.count(marker)==1
  page=page.replace(marker,marker+'<aside style="border-left:5px solid #a56521;background:#fff8e8;padding:14px"><b>Content review: '+html.escape(judgment)+'</b><p>'+html.escape(note)+'</p>'+('<p><b>Redesign check:</b> '+html.escape(extra)+'</p>' if extra else '')+'</aside>')
intro='<h1>v0.6 annotated content review</h1><p><b>Conclusion:</b> the eight targeted structural mismatches are substantially repaired, but shared psychological meaning is not established. Some measures remain compliance-heavy; others offer discretionary behavior. Eight scenarios have identical P1/P2 prompts. All findings are editorial, not model results. The original instrument is unchanged.</p>'
page=page.replace('<h1>v0.6 — full paired questions</h1>',intro)
for q,n in collections.Counter(r['question'] for r in rows).items():assert page.count('<p>'+html.escape(q)+'</p>')==n
(OUT/'annotated-side-by-side.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
report=dict(instrument_commit='f534003',questions_sha256=hashlib.sha256((B/'questions.csv').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),scope='42 profile pairs; editorial review, no model experiments',identical_first_stage_scenarios=identical_scenarios,identical_first_stage_cells=len(duplicates),pairs=audits)
(OUT/'audit.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf-8')
print('42 pairs annotated; all 648 exact question rows preserved; 16 duplicate-wording cells across 8 scenarios confirmed.')
